#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_delta

#% text
# `discrete_delta(n)` gives 1 when `n` is 0 and 0 when it is another number.

#% text
# `discrete_delta(n1, n2, ...)` gives 1 when every argument is 0 and 0 when one is a nonzero number.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With symbolic arguments the call stays.

#% item
# `kronecker_delta(n1, n2)` compares two arguments with each other instead.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_delta(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
discrete_delta(3)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
discrete_delta(n)
#% output
#= discrete_delta(n)

#% cell
table(discrete_delta(k - 2), k, range(0, 4))
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1, 0, 0]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% cell
z_transform(discrete_delta(n - 2), n, z)
#% output
#= z^-2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `kronecker_delta`, `dirac_delta`, `unit_step`, `z_transform`
